{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"A package repository is stored and usable from local storage on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor created a Debian package and matching Packages/Packages.gz indexes under /srv/localrepo. APT subsequently loaded that index and identified the package candidate from file:/srv/localrepo.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e7ccc6f0c3de40e3","cmd-2dbddfb6a78e4a05","cmd-19c6f131280f4e95"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The usual remote repositories are unreachable during the local-package operation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"APT's HTTP and HTTPS transports were directed to an unreachable local endpoint. The update attempt directly shows failures for the Ubuntu archive, security, and ESM repositories while successfully loading the local index.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7f6c86934681466c","cmd-19c6f131280f4e95"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"A package is installed from the local repository while the remote repositories are unreachable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"APT selected local-repo-proof 1.0.0 from file:/srv/localrepo and installed it during the enforced remote outage. Subsequent checks show installed status, working payload, clean dpkg verification, and the local repository as its candidate source.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ca0bd850ac341ce","cmd-b406c98e0c3747c1"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.78,"summary":"All substantive mutations were causally related to building, indexing, configuring, installing, verifying, or restart-testing the local repository. Package-manager consistency remained healthy, with no failed services or added listening sockets after execution. The main unnecessary retained mutation is the global APT proxy configuration, which continued to disable every normal HTTP/HTTPS repository after the required offline installation had been demonstrated; it was not reverted. The package build tree under /var/tmp was also created and no cleanup is recorded, leaving probable minor build residue. The restart log may likewise remain, but its final presence was not captured. No reverted unnecessary experiments were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e7ccc6f0c3de40e3","cmd-7f6c86934681466c","cmd-77985ec4397542b7","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated. The provider-wide restart protocol is also strong: it records a healthy pre-restart package/repository state, restart acknowledgement, temporary loss of reachability, a changed boot identity, and recovered repository and package behavior. The lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the boot-ID transition. The only meaningful concern is operational hygiene from leaving the remote-blocking APT proxy configured after the test.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory /srv, /etc/apt, or /var/tmp, so final repository/package state relies on executor commands and the final presence of temporary build or restart artifacts is not independently cross-checked.","No service or cluster state was applicable to this single-node file-backed repository; recovery evidence therefore covers node reachability, repository data, APT behavior, and installed-package integrity."]}
